All, here's my first non-explore-mode ascension.

Kenzie started exploring the dungeon with her cat Concatenation who
didn't last very long.  She found or converted a coaligned altar on
Dlvl 2 right next to the up stairs and declared it her main base. 
This level also had the entrance to the mines.  She worked her way
down, alternating between the branches, and found her first BoH. 
After a while, she felt safe tackling Sokoban for an "oR, then went
back and finished off the mines.

With that done, she went to the sink on Dlvl 3 and started pudding
dancing for items, and killing anything that was generated on Dlvl 2
for sacrificing.  When she learned turn undead, she hauled a pudding
fragment up to Dlvl 2 and began dancing up there instead so that she
could combine the two endeavors.

As she grew bored of a diet of pudding and frustrated with not finding
/WoW or a marker, she decided to descend further, completing her
quest, cleaning out Ludios, taking out Medusa, and claiming the /WoW
from the castle.  After wasting a few wishes on failed attempts at
PYEC, she turned to more practical wishes to contribute to her
ascension kit.  A bit more dancing and she dove down in progressive
stabs to the deepest level of the dungeon, killing Vlad along the way,
and found a curious vibrating square.  She then returned to her base,
clearing and lighting paths along the way.

After satisfying herself that she had sufficiently good
armour/weapons, etc, she dove again to tackle Rodney, the sanctum, and
then fly through the planes.

The journey was complicated by a few matters, the first of which was a
BoT in BoH accident that wiped out some spellbooks that were never
replaced as well as many other useful items.  The Dlvl 2 altar was
cursed twice by careless selection of sacrifices.  Toward the end, a
huge chunk of her kit was destroyed by a careless over-enchantment of
Magicbane and then putting on armour while on an E-square after
becoming lycanthropic.  At the very end, Thoth was angered by a
careless Finger of Death that took out the priestess attending his
high altar.

One particularly sticky moment was on the astral plane when a powerful
rogue appeared, wielding the +6 Vorpal Blade, which cost three amulets
of lifesaving (the fourth was used much earlier due to trying to take
a particular kind of corpse ungloved).

